    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d126">

                <pb facs="0178" n="168" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg168"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/3–2648: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-03-26T19:00:00+08:00">March 26, 1948—7
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 26—8:37 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>694. ReContels March 25, 470 to Embassy (669, to Department) and 676 to
                        Department<anchor n="44" xml:id="d126-f1"/> (476 to Embassy). On basis
                    preliminary study available information, we inclined toward view that: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Authorities have actually uncovered Communist organization operating
                            in local utilities and factories.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Those arrested probably include both genuine Communists and workers
                            unwittingly duped into identifying themselves with Communist
                            organization.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>Situation remains uneasy as result of anti-CC movement in labor unions
                            which has been aggravated by Communists, and of fear among laborers
                            resulting from their uncertainty whether their names are on list of
                            several hundred names of “Communists” which authorities have not yet
                            made public.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>Please pass to Military Attaché as combined report of ConGen and Assistant
                    Military Attaché.</p>
                <p>Sent Embassy as 487; repeated Department.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
